@@ -38,6 +38,7 @@
 ```{rubric} Misc
 ```
 
+- Require Python 3.13 or newer, following [SPEC 0](https://scientific-python.org/specs/spec-0000/), which drops Python 3.12 {pr}`881` {smaller}`S Dicks`
 - Deprecate `layer`, `obsm`, `use_rep`, `use_raw`, `neighbors_key`, `obsp`, `adjacency`, `key_added`, `batch_key`, `inplace` and `copy` in favor of `use`, `out` and `batch`, as scanpy 1.13 does; `filter_cells` and `filter_genes` keep `copy` {pr}`882` {smaller}`S Dicks`
 - Rename `mask_var`/`mask_obs` to `mask` in {func}`~rapids_singlecell.pp.pca`, {func}`~rapids_singlecell.pp.scale` and {func}`~rapids_singlecell.tl.rank_genes_groups`, which takes references such as `A.var["highly_variable"]` ([scverse/scanpy#4333](https://github.com/scverse/scanpy/pull/4333)) {pr}`882` {smaller}`S Dicks`
 - Make {func}`~rapids_singlecell.pp.calculate_qc_metrics` return its metrics by default under the `scanpy-v1` preset and write them under `scanpy-v2-preview`, as scanpy does; pass `out=False` to keep writing them {pr}`882` {smaller}`S Dicks`
